# The generalization gap: the published models scored on the rows they were fit on.
#
#     cd chtc && mkdir -p logs && condor_submit_dag gap.dag
#     ./fetch_results.sh --clean eval_xco2_gap_train eval_last4_gap_train \
#                                eval_profiles_gap_train
#
# WHAT THIS ANSWERS
# -----------------
# The question: "aren't there typically model diagnostics that can be used to demonstrate
# generalization?" The reference-disjoint and time-disjoint experiments answer the
# question of protocol -- the models are evaluated on scenes and months they never saw.
# What is still missing is the number an ML reader looks for first: the same metric on the
# training rows, so the gap between in-sample and out-of-sample can be read off directly
# instead of inferred.
#
# No training happens here. The checkpoints, the standardization constants, the Laplace
# fit (training partition) and its calibration (validation partition) are all the ones
# behind Table~\ref{tab:splitcompare}; the only thing that changes is which rows get
# scored, through EVAL_PARTITION. Each job draws 45 whole reference soundings of the
# training partition (EVAL_REFS=45 in eval_gap.sub) so its bootstrap standard errors are
# comparable with the 45 held-out ones.
#
# The ACOS L2FP rows are the control. The operational retrieval does not train, so its
# train-minus-test difference is the difficulty difference between the two partitions --
# expected to be near zero, since the split table's own variance structure is nearly
# identical on both sides (experiments/scoring/tables/generalization_partitions.csv:
# within-scene sd 1.825 vs 1.822 ppm, between-scene 2.558 vs 2.530 ppm). Whatever the two
# learned models do beyond that is fitting.
#
# Three short scoring jobs, no parents, ~20 minutes each.
#
# Prerequisites, all already in /staging for the published run (./fetch_results.sh --status):
#   oco2_processed_{train,test}.tar.gz, oco2_profile_stats.tar.gz   stage_data.sh
#   oco2_split_v1.tar.gz                                            prep.sub
#   oco2_covariates_v1.tar.gz                                       covariates.sub
#   results/<study>_final.tar.gz  for the six studies                bo/final.sub

JOB eval_xco2_gap      eval_gap.sub
VARS eval_xco2_gap      task="xco2"     det_study="det_xco2"     flow_study="nf_xco2"

JOB eval_last4_gap     eval_gap.sub
VARS eval_last4_gap     task="last4"    det_study="det_last4"    flow_study="nf_last4"

JOB eval_profiles_gap  eval_gap.sub
VARS eval_profiles_gap  task="profiles" det_study="det_profiles" flow_study="nf_profiles"

# A failed node should not stop the others; RETRY 0 for the reason given in balanced.dag.
RETRY ALL_NODES 0

NODE_STATUS_FILE gap.dag.status 30
